{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"a total of 50 new workers must be trained by the end of the 8th week,\" do you mean that 50 trainees must have completed their 2-week training (i.e., become productive workers) by the end of week 8, or that 50 trainees must have started training by the end of week 8 (some of whom would still be in training at week 8's end)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the definition of 'trained' (completion vs. start) by the deadline, which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can a skilled worker both train and produce in the same week, or must a skilled worker who is training be fully occupied with training and produce nothing during those weeks?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether a skilled worker can perform both training and production simultaneously, which constitutes one independent policy choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
